---

# 🎉 Python Fun Fact

Almost every web browser automatically sends dozens of HTTP headers whenever you open a website. APIs use these headers to understand and process requests correctly.

---

# 🔄 Quick Recap

- Headers are sent as a Python dictionary.
- `User-Agent` identifies the client.
- `Accept` tells the server which response format you prefer.
- Some APIs require an `Authorization` header for secure access.

